-- Q13244: Financial Valuation Methods [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under valuation principles consistent with ASC 820-10-35, FCFE represents cash flows available exclusively to equity holders after all debt obligations have been satisfied. The correct discount rate is the cost of equity (11%) because these cash flows already exclude debt service payments.
Wrong (A): WACC is appropriate for FCFF, where cash flows belong to all capital providers. Using WACC for FCFE would double-count the cost of debt.
Wrong (C): The cost of debt reflects the return required by lenders, not equity holders, and is irrelevant when discounting equity cash flows.
Wrong (D): A blended rate lacks theoretical justification and would produce an incorrect equity valuation.$EXPL$
