-- Q13247: Financial Valuation Methods [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 820-10-35-2 and enterprise valuation practice, minority interest (noncontrolling interest) is added to enterprise value because EV represents the total value of the firm to all capital providers. EV = Market cap + Debt + Minority interest - Cash = $200M + $50M + $10M - $15M = $245M. The consolidated statements include 100% of the subsidiary''s operations, so EV must reflect the minority holders'' claim.
Wrong (B): Subtracting minority interest would understate enterprise value by excluding a legitimate claim on the consolidated entity''s cash flows.
Wrong (C): Minority interest appears on the consolidated balance sheet precisely because it represents a real economic claim that must be included in EV.
Wrong (D): Minority interest is an equity-like claim on the subsidiary, not a cash offset; netting it against cash has no theoretical basis.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 13247;

