  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Per ASC 835-30-05 and macroeconomic theory, the crowding-out effect occurs when large-scale government borrowing competes with the private sector for loanable funds, driving up interest rates. The $180 billion decline in private investment results from higher borrowing costs caused by the government''s $500 billion entry into capital markets.
Wrong (A): The Phillips Curve describes the trade-off between inflation and unemployment, not the mechanism by which government borrowing displaces private investment.
