  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 820-10-55-3 and fixed income analytics, positive convexity means the price-yield relationship is curved, and the convexity adjustment (0.5 x convexity x change-in-yield-squared) is always positive regardless of rate direction. For the 200 bp decline: 0.5 x 85 x 0.02^2 = 1.7%, making the actual price increase approximately 16.1% versus the 14.4% duration-only estimate.
Wrong (A): Positive convexity benefits bondholders in both directions, gaining more than duration predicts when rates fall and losing less when rates rise.
