  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under ASC 820-10-35-18 and interest rate theory, the pure expectations theory (Economist A) holds that the yield curve reflects the market''s forecast of future short-term rates. Liquidity preference theory (Economist B) adds a term premium because investors demand extra compensation for holding longer-duration bonds. Market segmentation theory (Economist C) argues that supply and demand within each maturity segment independently determine rates.
